## Control {{controlId}}: Employ FIPS-Validated Cryptography to Protect the Confidentiality of CUI at Rest

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization employs FIPS-validated cryptography to protect CUI at rest within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through BitLocker Drive Encryption on managed endpoints and Microsoft-managed encryption for cloud-stored data, administered by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if bitLockerEnforced}}
**Endpoint Encryption:**
BitLocker Drive Encryption protects CUI at rest on {{deviceCount}} managed devices. Device compliance policies enforce full-disk encryption as a requirement for accessing organizational resources:
{{#if devices}}
{{#each devices}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{operatingSystem}}) — Compliant: {{#if isCompliant}}Yes{{else}}No{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{else}}
BitLocker encryption enforcement has not been confirmed across managed devices. Endpoint CUI-at-rest protection requires verification.
{{/if}}

{{#if compliancePolicyActive}}
**Compliance Enforcement:**
Intune compliance policy "{{policyName}}" requires BitLocker encryption on all managed endpoints. Non-compliant devices are blocked from accessing CUI resources via Conditional Access integration.
{{#if policies}}
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}**{{#if description}} — {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{else}}
Device compliance policies for encryption enforcement have not been configured.
{{/if}}

**Cloud Storage Encryption:**
M365 GCC High encrypts all data at rest using AES-256 with FIPS 140-2 validated cryptographic modules. SharePoint Online, OneDrive for Business, and Exchange Online mailbox data are encrypted at the file and database levels.

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine BitLocker deployment status, Intune compliance policy configurations, device encryption reports, and Microsoft FIPS 140-2 validation certificates.

